title: resolve() does not follow symlinks, so a link escapes files.root
updated: 2026-11-13T05:25:26Z
---

main.go:571-583: dot-dot traversal and absolute inputs are correctly contained because filepath.Join cleans them, but a symlink inside files.root pointing outside is followed for both read and write. Low priority on Windows where creating symlinks is privileged, real on the Linux dev box. Acceptance: EvalSymlinks on the resolved path before the prefix check, with a test for a link pointing out of the root.

From k89 (go directive 1.19 -> 1.26): under the new GODEBUG defaults (winsymlink/winreadlinkvolume) a fix based only on filepath.EvalSymlinks would miss Windows junctions, which are no longer followed. Cover junctions explicitly.
